# Android 10's platform policy dropped the stock 8.1 grant:
#   (allow init socket_device_27_0 (sock_file (create setattr unlink)))
# and now only gives init "relabelto" on socket_device's directory. The
# generic /dev/socket(/.*)? label in plat_file_contexts is still
# socket_device (a dev_type, not a file_type), so init can no longer create
# the sockets declared by vendor rc files:
#
#   vendor/etc/init/mtk_agpsd.rc:
#     socket agpsd  stream 660 gps system
#     socket agpsd2 stream 660 gps inet
#     socket agpsd3 stream 660 gps inet
#
# First OTA:
#   avc: denied { create } comm="init" name="agpsd" (also agpsd2/agpsd3)
#        scontext=u:r:init:s0 tcontext=u:object_r:socket_device:s0
#        tclass=sock_file permissive=0
#
# Restore the stock grant. This is narrower than making init permissive and
# mirror-exact to the rule the 8.1 vendor policy shipped. No AOSP neverallow
# covers init/socket_device:sock_file (only appdomain writes are forbidden).
allow init socket_device:sock_file { create setattr unlink };
